From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 14:17:02 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] RetroPlayer: register the FBO renderer on GBM

The upstream branch only registered CRendererFactoryFBO for Wayland, and
registered it ahead of the software renderers - which is why that branch also
had to disable the DMA renderer to stop the FBO pool capturing everything.
Registering it last, combined with the pool answering IsCompatible() honestly,
means an unactivated FBO pool cannot affect any software client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
index 74c991b..e48e893 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "OptionalsReg.h"
 #include "cores/RetroPlayer/process/gbm/RPProcessInfoGbm.h"
 #include "cores/RetroPlayer/rendering/VideoRenderers/RPRendererDMAOpenGLES.h"
+#include "cores/RetroPlayer/rendering/VideoRenderers/RPRendererFBO.h"
 #include "cores/RetroPlayer/rendering/VideoRenderers/RPRendererOpenGLES.h"
 #include "cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/DVDFactoryCodec.h"
 #include "cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.h"
@@ -66,6 +67,10 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::InitWindowSystem()
   RETRO::CRPProcessInfoGbm::Register();
   RETRO::CRPProcessInfoGbm::RegisterRendererFactory(new RETRO::CRendererFactoryDMAOpenGLES);
   RETRO::CRPProcessInfoGbm::RegisterRendererFactory(new RETRO::CRendererFactoryOpenGLES);
+  // Registered last: CRPRenderManager takes the first buffer pool that reports
+  // itself compatible, and the FBO pool only does so once a game client has
+  // asked for a hardware context
+  RETRO::CRPProcessInfoGbm::RegisterRendererFactory(new RETRO::CRendererFactoryFBO);
 
   // GLES 3.0 required for 10-bit texture format support (GL_RGB10_A2, GL_R16UI, etc.)
   // Fall back to GLES 2.0 for devices that don't support GLES 3.0 (e.g. lima driver)
